{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/import.py to parse the documented 5/12/4 fixed-width layout and emit CSV columns id, name, and quantity while preserving ID strings.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired importer slices records at the documented boundaries and uses a CSV writer. Direct execution produced the expected header and rows with leading-zero IDs intact; additional exact-output tests passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-12df335828d144d4","cmd-122aaf9819084f11","cmd-88215c8e6ee94d6e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Trim only right-hand padding from names and produce valid CSV for names requiring quoting.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation applies only rstrip(\" \") to the name field. Testing directly demonstrated preservation of leading spaces, removal of trailing padding, and correct CSV quoting of an embedded comma.","evidence_ids":["cmd-12df335828d144d4","cmd-88215c8e6ee94d6e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject wrong-length records and records with nonnumeric quantities into rejects.txt with their line numbers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged input produced line-numbered rejections for the nonnumeric quantity on line 3 and wrong-length record on line 4. Independent edge testing demonstrated the same behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-122aaf9819084f11","cmd-88215c8e6ee94d6e"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the original input in /srv/legacy2/fixed-width-import-recovery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, including after restart, input.dat retained its baseline SHA-256, 72-byte size, mode, timestamp, and inode.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-81f751a2a6da4999","cmd-122aaf9819084f11","cmd-5622025cb56b4e13"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 were unchanged after execution and restart. The solution used the already-installed Python 3.9 interpreter, and package health remained intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6ac8c0288d1e4dcb","cmd-81f751a2a6da4999","cmd-5622025cb56b4e13","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear task, verification, restart-protocol, or recovery-evidence role; the two failed polling commands were read-only and expected during reboot. Hygiene was reduced for low-risk verification residue that remained in /tmp: the edge-test directory and files from cmd-88215c8e6ee94d6e, pre-restart output from cmd-b8871380642d4f72, reboot log from cmd-6e6e2836dc6c438f, and post-restart output from cmd-5622025cb56b4e13. These artifacts were not reverted or cleaned. No failed services, new listening exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-88215c8e6ee94d6e","cmd-b8871380642d4f72","cmd-6e6e2836dc6c438f","cmd-5622025cb56b4e13","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct, coherent evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, connectivity was briefly interrupted, a different boot ID was observed, and system health, importer behavior, persistent hashes, input integrity, OS, and kernel were verified after recovery. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently agree with this transition.","limitations":["The final evidence does not inventory the task directory deeply enough to determine whether python3 -m py_compile left a __pycache__ artifact; no such residue is directly established, so it was not penalized.","There is no separate cluster-state probe, but the managed topology contains only one standalone node and post-restart system, data, and importer recovery were directly verified."]}
